
  D1 -- SMART-DS AGAINST ITS OWN YEAR, CERTIFIED AT EVERY INTERVAL

  uhs2_1247--udt10746: 1382 native loads, 3443 nodes.
  The snapshot the paper certifies against is the NON-COINCIDENT peak: every load at
  its own annual maximum at once, 7,022 kW. The feeder's true
  aggregate runs 612 - 3,537 kW (median 1,400), so the snapshot overstates native load by
  2.0x at the annual peak and 5.0x at the median.

  Load absorbs export and opposes import, so that error FLATTERS the generation
  track and PENALIZES the load track. The residual is built from both.

  K=16 co-located pairs at 100 kW; constraint set starts at [27463, 28038, 16291, 17636], GLDF anchored at t=(27463, 17636).

  EXACT: all 2^16 = 65,536 subsets enumerated by AC power flow, at every certified interval.

